[ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW]
pyramid:
  Layer 1: editor (executable)
            └── engine (static lib)
                  └── core (static lib)
                        └── common (INTERFACE)
                              └── third-party

[LAYER_HIERARCHY]
description: Dependency order (lower depends on higher)

[LAYER_COMMON]
role: Interfaces and third-party headers
provides:
  - GLM math library
  - Boost headers (json, hana, program_options, asio, test)
  - Custom data structures (fixed_vector, smart pointers)
  - Engine-wide macros and assertions
scope: Editor + Engine + Core

[LAYER_CORE]
role: Engine foundation and services
modules:
  - ecs: EnTT-based ECS with multi-world support (up to 8 worlds)
  - window: Platform window management
  - resource: VFS resolver, Adapter pipeline (Assimp/stb/text), cache
  - desc: JSON descriptor system with inheritance (level→world→prefab)
  - config: Macro-based config system (CFG_VAR_DEF_*)
  - app: Application lifecycle and module system
  - video: Window abstraction layer
key_patterns:
  - Service Locator: ds::app_data_storage (type-safe DI)
  - Module System: Priority-ordered lifecycle (CORE→ENGINE→EDITOR→GAME)
  - Resource System: res::tag identification, VFS protocols (res://,memory://)
  - Descriptor System: Inheritance chain, JSON serialization

[LAYER_ENGINE]
role: Gameplay and rendering systems
modules:
  - scene: Entity/prefab management, hierarchy, object transforms
  - render: Data-driven pipeline (extractors→passes), material system
  - gui: ImGui integration, editor panels
  - input: Keyboard/mouse/gamepad handling
  - game: Game-specific systems and logic hooks
render_pipeline:
  1. Extractors: Camera→RenderPacket (geometry, instances, lights)
  2. Passes: Shadow (depth), G-Buffer (normals, albedo, PBR), Lighting, Post-fx
  3. Output: ImGui overlay, multiple render targets per camera

[LAYER_EDITOR]
role: Real-time scene editing
modules:
  - editor: Main editor application
  - panels: Inspector, hierarchy, asset browser, prefab editor
  - gizmo: Transform, rotate, scale handles in viewport
  - viewport: Scene preview, camera controls
key_features:
  - Async operations (loading, cooking resources)
  - Per-camera render targets (__editor_depth_rt, etc.)
  - Live prefab preview in separate world
  - Descriptor hot-reload and validation

[MEMORY_SYSTEM]
allocators:
  - frame_allocator: Per-frame bump (resets every frame start)
  - linear_resource: Custom-scoped bump allocator
  - pool_resource: Fixed-size O(1) alloc/free
  - stack_resource: LIFO with markers
  - debug_resource: Guard bytes, leak tracking (Debug only)
hot_path_pattern:
  std::pmr::vector<T> vec(ds::frame_allocator());
  vec.reserve(estimated_size); // avoid grow-copy
  // use vec during frame
  // automatically freed at frame reset

[ECS_SYSTEM]
worlds: Up to 8 independent worlds (world_salt + bind_res<WorldID,T>)
systems: All inherit ecs::system_interface, auto-registered via system_factory
components: POD structs, optional _component suffix
dependency_resolution: Auto via invoker<Candidate> using registry context
boot_sequence:
  module_loader.add_module(core, engine, editor)
  → register_all_services()
  → initialize_all_services() // sorted by priority
  → app.run() // game loop
  → shutdown_all_services() // reverse order

[RESOURCE_SYSTEM]
identification: res::tag (unique resource identifier)
protocols:
  - res:// filesystem (VFS resolver)
  - memory:// runtime data
pipeline:
  VFS Resolver → Adapter (Assimp/stb/text) → Cache (weak/pinned)
async_loading: res_handle<T> with .then() callbacks
caching: Weak refs (auto-unload), pinned (persistent)

[DESCRIPTOR_SYSTEM]
format: JSON files (.desc extension)
inheritance_chain:
  level_desc
    └── world_desc (entities, systems config)
          └── prefab_desc (reusable template)
                └── prefab_node (hierarchy)
                      └── prefab_comp_node (component data)
hot_reload: Editors change descs → scene updates via binding
validation: Type checking, circular dep detection

[RENDER_PIPELINE_DETAIL]
per_camera:
  - color_targets: fixed_vector<4> MRT support
  - depth_target, tp_accum_target, tp_reveal_target
  - RT tags resolve from camera packet, fallback to legacy static tags

passes:
  - Shadow Pass: Depth rendering for lights
  - G-Buffer Pass: Normal, albedo, PBR encoding
  - Lighting Pass: Deferred shading
  - Transparency Pass: OIT (Order-Independent Transparency)
  - Post-FX Pass: Bloom, tone mapping, etc.
  - ImGui Pass: Editor UI overlay

[MODULE_LIFECYCLE]
Each module implements app::modules::module_interface:

1. register_services(): Add types to app_data_storage
   - Constructor injection, no dependencies yet

2. initialize_services(): Resolve from storage, setup
   - Sorted by priority
   - Dependencies already registered

3. shutdown_services(): Cleanup in reverse order
   - Guaranteed to run even on error

[NAMING_PATTERNS]
namespaces: 2-4 letter abbrev (ds, ecs, scn, gui, rnd, res, inp, edt, gs, cfg, wnd)
files: prefix_name.hpp/.cpp (scn_renderer.hpp, res_loader.cpp)
components: _component suffix if name not self-descriptive
systems: Inherit system_interface, naming_system.cpp pattern
variables: snake_case always
macros: UPPER_CASE
